# Copy to .env. Everything the app reads from the environment is listed here;
# nothing else is. Values in .env never leave the machine — the file is
# ignored by git, and only this example is committed.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The running app connects through DATABASE_URL. Migrations, seeding, and the
# DB and browser test suites take DIRECT_URL. Against Neon these differ (the
# pooled endpoint cannot reliably run DDL); against a local Postgres they are
# the same string.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/cable_rqf
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/cable_rqf

# ── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs every session cookie. At least 32 characters, and never the example
# value — the app refuses to start on a placeholder. `openssl rand -base64 32`.
AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Reading uploaded PDFs (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset, the app still works: spreadsheets and pasted text are read locally,
# and a PDF opens as text with a note saying why. Set, the text of an uploaded
# PDF is sent to Google's Gemini API — read ARCHITECTURE.md §8 before pointing
# this at a customer's document.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# EXTRACTION_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=

# ── Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm test` needs none of this. `pnpm test:db` and `pnpm test:e2e` need the
# database above, migrated (`pnpm db:migrate`) and seeded (`pnpm db:seed`).
#
# The browser tests use the Chromium Playwright installs (`pnpm exec
# playwright install chromium`). On a machine that already has one and cannot
# download another, point at it:
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium

# ── Development only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run the app on in-memory repositories with no database at all.
# USE_MEMORY_ADAPTER=1
